meta {
  name: SetBudget
  type: grpc
  seq: 2
}

grpc {
  url: {{coreGrpc}}
  method: /dop.v1.CostService/SetBudget
  body: grpc
  auth: none
}

metadata {
  x-actor-id: {{actorId}}
  x-account-id: {{accountId}}
  x-request-id: {{$guid}}
}

body:grpc {
  [
    {
      "budget": {
        "scope": "demand",
        "scope_id": "{{demandId}}",
        "limit_micros": "5000000",
        "currency": "USD"
      }
    }
  ]
}

docs {
  The value is in MICROS (10⁻⁶ of the currency), an integer — never a float. A
  token costs a fraction of a cent; in cents every record would round to zero, and
  a float accumulates error over a sum of millions of rows.

  `limit_micros: 0` is NO CEILING, not a zero ceiling.

  Exceeding the budget PAUSES the demand and becomes an item in the attention box —
  it does not kill work in progress (ADR-0008 §2).
}
